    "stability_amendment": "Before D production outcomes, repeated D pilot runs showed configuration-specific bounded runtime cadence or settling in E16 at GBS32/128 and E32 at GBS32/64/128. All affected 134,217,728-token probes retained finite loss and gradients, exact token and full-state checkpoint accounting, zero skipped or NaN iterations, zero dropped tokens, safe allocated and observed VRAM, and p99/median step-time ratios below 1.28. Scoped 8%, 10%, or 12% CV limits plus a stricter p99/median below 1.35 guard distinguish bounded system cadence from hangs or pathological stalls without weakening any correctness, memory, token-accounting, checkpoint, or MoE-routing gate.",
    "gpu_hour_limit": 3200.0,
    "gpu_hour_limit_amendment": "Before D production outcomes, the clean 2026-07-23 R5 D preflight measured the complete frozen grid at 3036.88 conservative H100-hours after the 0.90 throughput safety factor, all seven mandatory 20% cooldown branches, evaluation, checkpoint, and control overhead. The D-only launch cap is therefore corrected from 2500 to 3200 H100-hours. This cost-only amendment remains below the six-node reservation's gross capacity and changes no model, data, token, learning-rate, checkpoint, evaluation, or ladder-cell contract."
